			"properties:10": {
				"betterquesting:10": {
					"notification_pos_y:3": -2147483648,
					"notification_subtitle_scale:5": -1.0,
					"visibility:8": "NORMAL",
					"notification_style:8": "default",
					"notification_duration:5": -1.0,
					"completion_particle:8": "default",
					"isMain:1": 0,
					"lockedProgress:1": 0,
					"repeat_relative:1": 1,
					"notification_fade_out:5": -1.0,
					"snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",
					"repeatTime:3": -1,
					"notification_pos_x:3": -2147483648,
					"particle_count:3": -1,
					"countAsQuest:1": 1,
					"autoClaim:1": 0,
					"globalShare:1": 0,
					"desc:8": "The Pattern Repeater is a niche but useful tool. It allows recipes to be visible across networks.\n\nWhen two networks are linked via a repeater, you could have a pattern that lives on network A and be able to see it in network B. In practice, you could request the item from network B (using items from network B), then those items would be transferred to the pattern destination on network A, and the resulting item would end up on network B when completed.\n\nIn order to set this up, simply make a pair of Pattern Repeaters (attached to separate networks) face into one another. You can then use a wrench to toggle each to the desired mode: either Provider or Accessor. You will need one of each.\n\nThe \"§5Accessor§r\" side is where the original pattern should sit. It will \"send\" the pattern to the other network. §3(Network A in the example above)§r\n\nThe \"§5Provider§r\" side is where the pattern is provided to. It \"receives\" the incoming pattern from the other network. §3(Network B in the example above)§r",
					"notification_icon_scale:5": -1.0,
					"notification_show_icon:8": "default",
					"notification_fade_in:5": -1.0,
					"icon:10": {
						"id:8": "appliedenergistics2:item.ItemMultiPart",
						"Count:3": 1,
						"Damage:2": 473,
						"OreDict:8": ""
					},
					"isSilent:1": 0,
					"notification_subtitle:8": "",
					"snd_update:8": "random.levelup",
					"questLogic:8": "AND",
					"name:8": "Pattern Repeater",
					"simultaneous:1": 0,
					"taskLogic:8": "AND",
