					"notification_style:8": "default",
					"notification_duration:5": -1.0,
					"completion_particle:8": "default",
					"isMain:1": 0,
					"lockedProgress:1": 0,
					"repeat_relative:1": 1,
					"notification_fade_out:5": -1.0,
					"snd_complete:8": "random.levelup",
					"repeatTime:3": -1,
					"notification_pos_x:3": -2147483648,
					"particle_count:3": -1,
					"countAsQuest:1": 1,
					"autoClaim:1": 0,
					"globalShare:1": 0,
					"desc:8": "Genetics has its own little glassware for carrying chosen genes over to Larvae. The Serum Vial will let you carry one gene to a Larvae. That's kind of underwhelming, so it's better to combine a few of them into a Serum Array. Then you can have a full buffet and pick one of each possible trait.\n\nYou must \"charge\" the Serum in a Polymerizer. Then you can feed it into an Inoculator or a Splicer to modify a Larvae. Look at the number of charges left on the Serum to see how many times you can do this. You can recharge it by putting it back in a Polymerizer. So if you ever get a magic recipe, you can just leave a Serum Array of it around and just recharge it as you need it.\n\n[note]You cannot recharge Serums using a Thaumic Restorer.[/note]",
					"notification_icon_scale:5": -1.0,
					"notification_show_icon:8": "default",
					"notification_fade_in:5": -1.0,
