					"globalShare:1": 1,
					"desc:8": "Regular chests can fill up rather quickly if you happen to collect mob drops like swords and/or armor. By using a cabinet, you can store up to 270 items of the same type. Also, it doesn't need a dolly - you can break it normally and it will retain contents.\n\nPerfect for storing Forestry saplings, bees, or really anything that shares an ID but won't stack because of NBT!\n\n[note]Due to a bug in Extra Utilities, Filing Cabinets may incorrectly accept stackable and non-stackable items with different item IDs. To ensure that your cabinets contain only the items you want to store, use an item filter when inserting items through automation.[/note]",
